WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:01.949
- Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:03.242
I'm here with Kali Reis.

00:00:03.242 --> 00:00:04.109
Give it up!

00:00:04.109 --> 00:00:06.302
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:06.302 --> 00:00:09.057
So, it is the countdown
to the Paris Olympics

00:00:09.057 --> 00:00:10.320
and my next guest

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.750
is one of the most
anticipated athletes to watch.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.240
She is a two-time Olympic gold medalist,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.320
and current world record holder
in the 400 meter hurdles.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.580
Despite her success, though,

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.310
she has struggled with
anxiety and insecurity,

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.087
something she writes
about in her new book,

00:00:25.087 --> 00:00:27.840
"Far Beyond Gold: Running
From Fear to Faith."

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.728
Everybody, please welcome
Sydney McLaughlin-Levrone.

00:00:30.728 --> 00:00:34.811
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:40.715 --> 00:00:45.632
(audience cheering and clapping continues)

00:00:49.181 --> 00:00:50.098
Hello!
- Hi.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.013
- Meet another exceptional athlete.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.620
And then, meet another
exceptional athlete.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.790
No, I'm just kidding.
- Amazing.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:57.690
- I was saying this show

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.250
is making me inferior as a human.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.950
I was like, "Wow,
everyone, athletic today."

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.030
We need to set this up.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:06.720
So Sydney is the first
woman to break 52 seconds

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.296
in the 400 meter hurdles.

00:01:08.296 --> 00:01:11.370
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:15.420
She is also the first to break 51 seconds.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:20.420
In fact, this is crazy, of the
10 fastest times in history,

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.949
history, Sydney holds
six of those records.

00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:28.688
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.633
You're dominating.

00:01:30.633 --> 00:01:32.520
Like that's incredible.
- Thank you.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:35.010
- I would feel like Captain Marvel.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.030
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.400
- Do you feel good about
going into the Olympics?

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.233
Do you feel good about where you're at?

00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:40.110
- I do.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:43.560
Listen, the competition
is insane every year,

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.830
so you always have to respect
your competitors, obviously.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:49.080
Feeling good, but the
target is always on my back.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.030
So just getting prepared for that.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.880
- Do you though, 'cause, nothing like you,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.720
but I did grow up in sports,

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.137
and I loved that the
coaches were always like,

00:01:56.137 --> 00:01:57.270
"Compete against yourself

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:58.890
and your best time."
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.450
- [Kelly] So do you
think about that more so?

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:04.290
- Yeah, I mean, I try to run my own race.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.870
Worry about my 10 hurdles,
worry about my lane.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.360
Yeah, you can't get focused
on what everyone else is doing

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.040
'cause everyone has a different process.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:14.310
And so, for me, every day
it's, "How can I beat myself?"

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:18.300
- Yeah, was Olympic boxing,
is that ever a dream?

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.100
It still can be, you do all the things.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.320
- Well, fun fact, I know, fun fact,

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.840
women's boxing wasn't in
the Olympics until 2012.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.580
So I went pro in 2008,

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:27.663
and there was no-

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.240
- [Kelly] Avenue for that.
- There was no avenue.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.010
So, I could do all the
amateur tournaments,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.510
but financially I couldn't make 'em

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.130
so I just decided to go pro.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.510
The day after I decided to go pro,

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.220
I heard they were put in
boxing in the Olympics.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.410
But everything happens for a reason,

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.000
and I'm glad they have it now,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:42.990
'cause there's so many opportunities

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:45.810
and I see so many young women
coming up in the amateur ranks

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.430
and getting so much experience.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.330
- I didn't know that.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.977
You are giving me all the information.

00:02:49.977 --> 00:02:51.540
♪ The more you know ♪

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.860
Well, I heard this about you too,

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.510
you juggle before meets.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:55.980
Is this true?
- I do.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.140
- Is this like a meditation thing?

00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.100
Like a therapeutic thing?

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.990
- Yeah, juggling is actually really good,

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.000
number one, for like calming you down.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.470
It gives you something else to focus on,

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:06.570
it's really good for
hand-eye coordination,

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:08.460
and it's a really good party trick

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.800
that you can just pull
out anywhere, so yeah.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.920
- Yeah, that's an amazingly random thing,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.240
but I love that everybody has their thing.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.650
Did you ever have
anything you'd have to do

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.620
like to settle yourself
before going in the ring?

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.100
- I like kind of a calm,
funny, chill vibe in the back.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.220
But like I bring my ceremonial ways,

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.810
I guess you could say, into the ring.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.180
I usually have traditional
dancers and drummers

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.650
bring me out to the ring.

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.270
It's an honor to my heritage,

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.680
and kind of just that collective energy

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.120
to put that healing vibe out.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.040
And it is kind of a cool perspective.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.770
- Yeah, oh, it's very cool.
- Yeah.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:43.020
- Writing a book, I can't imagine like,

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.003
not into the idea personally,

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.120
'cause it has to be hard and vulnerable.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:48.953
- For sure.
- What do you think

00:03:48.953 --> 00:03:50.760
was the most challenging
part of writing the book?

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.890
- Man, I mean, the point of the book,

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.990
I've struggled with fear my whole life,

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.420
kind of just my identity,
and being a winner,

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.640
and obviously that's not
guaranteed in this life.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.770
And I think I'm very grateful to God

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.990
for setting me free from
that by way of Jesus Christ.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.100
- Yeah.
- And my goal with the book

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.680
was really just to encourage
readers to seek Him,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.083
and seek that freedom
that is far beyond gold.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.750
And the hardest part I would say

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.440
is just being honest with my
past, and my own insecurities,

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.510
and things that I maybe didn't do right.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.190
But being able to own that,

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.430
and show that with Christ we
are forgiven from those things.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:26.310
- It is a lot of weight to
put on a 17-year-old kid.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.960
You know, you're saying
you're 17 years old

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.060
and, like, I can't even imagine.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.127
Like, even the hormones
that are happening at 17,

00:04:32.127 --> 00:04:32.960
you know what I'm saying?

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.100
And then, also trying
to do something so huge,

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.390
and so much pressure.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.950
That's a lot.
- Absolutely.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:38.783
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:38.783 --> 00:04:40.200
- [Kelly] Keep juggling.
- Keep juggling.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.150
- Yeah, that's what I say.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:45.060
I can't wait to juggle at lunch
just to see if I can do it.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.920
Sydney's book, "Far Beyond Gold:

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.150
Running From Fear to Faith,"

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.380
is available right now, everybody.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:50.760
Be sure to pick up a copy.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.670
And you can cheer for Sydney
and Team USA this summer.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:56.763
Watch the Paris Olympics
on NBC and Peacock.

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:57.732
We'll be right back.

00:04:57.732 --> 00:05:00.399
(upbeat music)

